{
  "id": "m05-range-sum-queries",
  "title": "Range Sum Queries",
  "source": {
    "name": "Standard prefix-sum exercise; compare CSES 'Static Range Sum Queries'",
    "url": "https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1646"
  },
  "rating": 900,
  "tags": [
    "prefix-sums",
    "arrays"
  ],
  "statement": "You are given an array of `n` integers and `q` queries. Each query gives two indices `l` and `r` (1-indexed, inclusive). For each query print the sum of the elements from position `l` to position `r`.\n\n**Input.** First line `n` and `q`. Second line the `n` integers. Then `q` lines, each `l r`.\n\n**Output.** `q` lines, one sum per query.\n\n**Example.**\n\nInput:\n```\n5 3\n1 2 3 4 5\n1 5\n2 4\n3 3\n```\nOutput:\n```\n15\n9\n3\n```",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n, q ≤ 800 in this browser version (the idea scales to 2·10^5)",
    "−10^9 ≤ each value ≤ 10^9",
    "1 ≤ l ≤ r ≤ n"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 1000,
  "tests": [
    {
      "input": "5 3\n1 2 3 4 5\n1 5\n2 4\n3 3\n",
      "output": "15\n9\n3\n",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "input": "1 1\n-5\n1 1\n",
      "output": "-5\n",
      "hidden": false
    },
